			<div class="content" id="post-content-4271416">
									

<div style="text-align: center;">
<p><em>I like black and white</em><br />
<em>Dream in black in white</em><br />
<em>You like black and white</em><br />
<em>Run runaway</em></p>
</div>
<hr />
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoilers&nbsp;Abound,&nbsp;Come&nbsp;Come&nbsp;Around!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoiled&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;Day,&nbsp;Run&nbsp;Run&nbsp;Away!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>SCP-4229 is alive, a memette. The episodes were originally wholesome, and cheerful, but when Karma Kameleon was re-sold to Oliver Brothers Inc. to turn it into an imagination-killer, the content of the episodes began to change. The &quot;Hollow Men&quot; are Oliver Brothers Inc., the &quot;Sad Machines&quot; are the tools they used to destroy the &quot;Rainbow Forest&quot;, representing the memette's original purpose. Karma Kameleon, the character, is a visual representation of the memette, and the final episode, Karma taken from the forest and put in a cage, represents the results of it's torture.</p>
<p>The &quot;dream damage&quot;, half of which affects the human population to this day, was just a side-effect of this whole affair. If every episode had made it to air? Well, 05-4 describes it best.</p>
<p>Props to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/greytoiletpaper" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5426426); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5426426&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1564674499" alt="greytoiletpaper" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5426426)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/greytoiletpaper" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5426426); return false;">greytoiletpaper</a></span> for first commenting on this!</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<p>My second article here, after the truly wonderful reception I received for <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-4281">Stalled Conversation</a>. I hope you enjoy reading it!</p>
<p>Image was taken and edited personally.</p>
<p>Big thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/n-aepic-fael" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4463776); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4463776&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1564674499" alt="N_Aepic_Fael" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4463776)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/n-aepic-fael" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4463776); return false;">N_Aepic_Fael</a></span> for their in-depth crit! Also <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/crashington" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5028224); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5028224&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1564674499" alt="Crashington" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5028224)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/crashington" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5028224); return false;">Crashington</a></span> for catching some errors! <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rattles" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4377609); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4377609&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1564674499" alt="rattles" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4377609)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rattles" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4377609); return false;">rattles</a></span> for a review, If we traded drafts, please let me know!</p>
